Relevant columns and their potential usage  
body:  search within the article text for occurrences of the word “education”.  
title: search within the headline for occurrences of the word “education”.  
category: group articles and compute totals / percentages per section.  
filename: could act as a unique identifier when counting rows (not strictly required for this task).

Typical string‑matching condition  
WHERE LOWER(body)     LIKE '%education%'  
   OR LOWER(title)    LIKE '%education%'  

Below are ten different exploratory → analytical queries (each capped with LIMIT 20) that move from the simplest inspection to the final percentage computation.

```sql
-- 1) Description: List the distinct news categories that exist in the table.
SELECT DISTINCT `category`
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.bbc_news.fulltext`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Show 20 random rows (filename, category) for a quick glance.
SELECT `filename`, `category`
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.bbc_news.fulltext`
ORDER BY RAND()
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Count total number of articles in the full table.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_article_count
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.bbc_news.fulltext`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Count total number of articles that mention “education” in title or body.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS education_article_count
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.bbc_news.fulltext`
WHERE  LOWER(`body`)  LIKE '%education%'
   OR  LOWER(`title`) LIKE '%education%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Show 20 example articles that match the “education” keyword, displaying title/body snippet.
SELECT `filename`,
       `category`,
       SUBSTR(`title`,  1, 120) AS title_snippet,
       SUBSTR(`body`,   1, 120) AS body_snippet
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.bbc_news.fulltext`
WHERE  LOWER(`body`)  LIKE '%education%'
   OR  LOWER(`title`) LIKE '%education%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Count of articles per category (top 20 categories by volume).
SELECT `category`,
       COUNT(*) AS total_in_category
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.bbc_news.fulltext`
GROUP  BY `category`
ORDER  BY total_in_category DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Count of “education”‑mentioning articles per category.
SELECT `category`,
       COUNT(*) AS education_mentions
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.bbc_news.fulltext`
WHERE  LOWER(`body`)  LIKE '%education%'
   OR  LOWER(`title`) LIKE '%education%'
GROUP  BY `category`
ORDER  BY education_mentions DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Combine total and education counts side‑by‑side for each category.
SELECT
  `category`,
  COUNT(*)                                        AS total_in_category,
  SUM( CASE WHEN LOWER(`body`) LIKE '%education%'
             OR  LOWER(`title`) LIKE '%education%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END ) AS education_mentions
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bbc_news.fulltext`
GROUP BY `category`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Add percentage of articles mentioning education in each category.
SELECT
  `category`,
  COUNT(*)                                                          AS total_in_category,
  SUM( CASE WHEN LOWER(`body`) LIKE '%education%'
             OR  LOWER(`title`) LIKE '%education%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END ) AS education_mentions,
  ROUND( 100 * SUM( CASE WHEN LOWER(`body`) LIKE '%education%'
                          OR  LOWER(`title`) LIKE '%education%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END )
           / COUNT(*), 2)                                             AS pct_with_education
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bbc_news.fulltext`
GROUP BY `category`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Final answer – full breakdown of categories, totals, and education percentages (ordered by percentage desc).
SELECT
  `category`,
  COUNT(*)                                                          AS total_in_category,
  SUM( CASE WHEN LOWER(`body`) LIKE '%education%'
             OR  LOWER(`title`) LIKE '%education%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END ) AS education_mentions,
  ROUND( 100 * SUM( CASE WHEN LOWER(`body`) LIKE '%education%'
                          OR  LOWER(`title`) LIKE '%education%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END )
           / COUNT(*), 2)                                             AS pct_with_education
FROM `bigquery-public-data.bbc_news.fulltext`
GROUP BY `category`
ORDER BY pct_with_education DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
